Story 11: Build generated script validation layer

Story Points: 4

Description:
Implement a validation layer that checks generated scripts before deployment. The goal is to catch missing inputs, malformed script content, unsupported placeholders, or required steps that were not rendered correctly. This provides confidence that template-generated output is safe and usable before AWS deployment.

Acceptance Criteria:
	•	Validation checks for unresolved placeholders
	•	Validation checks for required sections based on template type
	•	Invalid scripts are blocked from deployment
	•	User receives clear validation errors
	•	Validation can run independently from deployment

